{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "eval.2026-09-08-reflow-152600.code-review-agents",
  "title": "Multi-agent automated code review",
  "description": "# Multi-agent automated code review\nRead left to right: PR intake resolves the diff, files, policy and build status; draft and generated/vendor filtering precedes ranked, budgeted context construction. The planner fans out shared context and review units to five concurrent reviewers (correctness and security only when the daily repository budget is exceeded). Reviewers have read-only tools and return available findings when their call budget expires.\n\nResults merge, deduplicate and reconcile severity, then undergo confidence and current-head location screening. High-severity findings are checked against source; unverified findings are demoted and not published. Survivors become inline comments and a policy-dependent summary verdict.\n\nThe lower control lane shows head-change cancellation, discarded partial work and restart against the new head; telemetry tracks reviewer usage and outcome metrics. Human feedback feeds calibration thresholds for subsequent screening.",
  "mode": "diagram",
